<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.3.4"/>
    <code code="10164-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="History of Present illness Narrative"/>
    <title>History of Present Illness</title>
    <text><paragraph>Mr. Paige returns five weeks after a moderate exacerbation treated at home with prednisone and doxycycline, and five days after finishing pulmonary rehabilitation (twenty sessions). He used his action plan well: he called the clinic the morning his breathing worsened and started treatment that day. He is back to walking to the store and beyond without stopping and uses albuterol about twice a week. He takes his inhaler every morning. He had his vaccines at the wellness visit three weeks ago with only a sore arm. His aortic ultrasound a week ago showed no aneurysm, and his hepatitis C and hepatitis B tests were negative. He asked whether he needs another inhaler after the flare-up. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Symptoms</td><td>CAT 11; mMRC 1</td></tr><tr><td>Exacerbations</td><td>One moderate, five weeks ago, treated at home; no hospital stay</td></tr><tr><td>Six-minute walk</td><td>425 m, from 360; lowest saturation 92 percent</td></tr><tr><td>Mood</td><td>PHQ-9 2</td></tr><tr><td>Screening results</td><td>Aorta 2.4 cm; hepatitis C and B negative</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
</component>

