    <text><table><thead><tr><th>Problem</th><th>Clinical status</th><th>Verification</th><th>Code</th><th>Provenance</th></tr></thead><tbody>
  <tr ID="problem-1">
    <td>Breathlessness on exertion for about two years, now after one flight of stairs or a block on the level (mMRC 2), with a morning cough and a little clear sputum most days; no chest pain, ankle swelling, orthopnea, wheeze at rest or weight loss; a former smoker of about 30 pack-years; cause under evaluation with spirometry and a pulmonology consultation</td><td>resolved</td><td>confirmed</td>
    <td>R06.09</td><td>S — Synthetic presenting problem anchored to his documented emphysema; superseded when spirometry at the consultation confirmed COPD.</td>
  </tr>
  <tr ID="problem-2">
    <td>Chronic obstructive pulmonary disease, GOLD grade 2 (post-bronchodilator FEV1/FVC 0.58, FEV1 61% predicted by the race-neutral GLI Global equations), GOLD group B (CAT 18, mMRC 2, no exacerbation in the past year); alpha-1 antitrypsin normal; blood eosinophils 0.08 x 10^3/uL; synthetic modern diagnosis linked to his documented emphysema</td><td>active</td><td>confirmed</td>
    <td>J44.9</td><td>S — Synthetic modern diagnosis made at the consultation, anchored to his documented emphysema; its onset and course in the modern episode are synthetic.</td>
  </tr>
  <tr ID="problem-3">
    <td>Former cigarette smoker, about 30 pack-years, stopped eleven years ago on his own; no use since</td><td>active</td><td>confirmed</td>
    <td>Z87.891</td><td>S — Synthetic smoking history: whether he smoked is not documented in the sources read, so the history is synthetic and labeled as such.</td>
  </tr>
  <tr ID="problem-4">
    <td>Hyperlipidemia: LDL 148 mg/dL, HDL 44 and triglycerides 160 at intake; estimated 10-year cardiovascular risk about 18 percent; atorvastatin started by shared decision</td><td>active</td><td>confirmed</td>
    <td>E78.5</td><td>S — Synthetic cardiovascular risk factor anchored to his documented heart trouble; not a claim about his real lipids.</td>
  </tr>
  <tr ID="problem-5">
    <td>Moderate exacerbation of COPD with a viral cold: more breathlessness, more sputum turning green, and wheeze for three days; oxygen saturation 92 percent; no pneumonia on chest X-ray; treated at home with prednisone and doxycycline; recovered</td><td>resolved</td><td>confirmed</td>
    <td>J44.1</td><td>S — Synthetic exacerbation at the sick visit; not a historical claim.</td>
  </tr></tbody></table></text>

